hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22693","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: I was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani when two youths of the children of Umar entered and prayed two rak'ahs after Asr, so he sent to them and called them, and said: What is this prayer you prayed, while your father used to forbid it? They said: A'ishah, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with her, narrated to us that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed them with her. So he was silent and did not return anything to them."
